From 1c4207cc59f9402427da1a41c8cacb0d0ce31a95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 21:59:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: keyboard notification commands in the shade

DESIGN-KF-A keyboard-first notification interaction for a focused
notification row: Space expands/collapses (it no longer opens), R opens
the source's RemoteInput reply when the row shows one, D dismisses, Z
opens snooze, M opens the delivery options (Android's NotificationInfo),
C opens the notification's Android channel/conversation settings, and H
asks Sable Hub to open the notification when Hub is installed.

Commands are contextual: they act only when the row itself has focus,
never with a modifier held, and a focused text editor (inline reply)
always receives printable keys. Arrows, Enter and Back keep their
existing paths. Each command reuses an existing SystemUI path
(performDismiss, the long-press menu, the RemoteInput button,
NotificationActivityStarter, which dismisses the keyguard first), so no
notification policy changes here.
